franka_meshes

This package holds mesh files that PickNik Inc. derived from Franka Robotics'
franka_description geometry. The two kinds of attribution below are separate and
must stay separate: the authorship of the derivation is PickNik's, and the
copyright in the source geometry is Franka Robotics'.


PickNik's own work in this package
----------------------------------

Copyright 2026 PickNik Inc.

Authored by PickNik Inc. No file here is an upstream franka_description file,
and nothing here is or should be attributed to Franka Robotics' own authorship.

- The *_convex_NN.stl files under meshes/*/collision/ are an approximate convex
  decomposition by PickNik Inc. of five franka_description collision meshes:
  the FR3 v2 link3, link4 and link5, the Franka head and the FR3 Duo mount.
  MuJoCo collides a mesh as its convex hull, so a mesh whose own shape is far
  from convex collides as the filled-in shape; each part written here is already
  convex, so hulling it changes nothing and the union of the parts follows the
  real shape. Every part carries "Modified by PickNik Inc. - convex collision
  part" in its 80-byte binary STL header.

- The *_visual.obj files under meshes/*/visual/ were converted by PickNik Inc.
  from the correspondingly named visual/*.dae meshes of franka_description with
  trimesh 4.12.2 and pycollada 0.9.3. The conversion is needed because MuJoCo
  has no COLLADA decoder. The converted files are modified: the submeshes of
  each source file are merged into a single mesh, duplicate vertices are merged,
  meshes above 30000 faces are decimated to that cap, the per-material COLLADA
  colours are dropped because a MuJoCo geom carries one colour, and
  franka_spine_visual.obj is scaled from its source's millimetres to metres.

